# tally 2.3.1 rulings 22 (5; L §5.19): a row whose kind lacks a leg of the move its fulfils names is refused at
# load, LOAD-LEG, on the rows that stand. The critic's P1-C4. Before: RUN-RECORD at every reader.
=== l1_lacks.tally
model l1
  tally 2
  on 2026-05-20
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "invented values"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
index month = month 2026-01..2026-03
kind paid: event certain
  leg cash: PLN
  leg fee: PLN
place pot: accounts PLN lives 2026-01-01..
place landlord: outside lives 1900-01-01..
place bankfees: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input bank: observed
input rent_amt: money PLN
input fee_amt: money PLN
input d5: int

move rent[m in month]: paid
  on day_of(m, d5)
  at start_of(m)
  leg cash from pot to landlord amount rent_amt
  leg fee from pot to bankfees amount fee_amt

ask c: bal(pot, 2026-01-31)
ask fb: flows(rent.fee, 2026-01-01..2026-03-31)
ask fr: flows(rent.fee, 2026-01)
ask rs: residuals pot 2026-01

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  rent_amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  fee_amt = 5.00 PLN "s"
  d5 = 5 "s"
  opening[pot] = 9000.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

version jan
  cite s
  governs 2026-01
  known 2026-02-01
  covers pot
  bank[a1] = (on: 2026-01-05, kind: transfers, leg cash from pot to landlord amount 100.00 PLN, fulfils: rent[2026-01]) "names jan"
=== expect
refused: LOAD-LEG observation bank[a1] fulfils rent[2026-01] and lacks its leg fee (l1_lacks.tally:46)
